Z||000012||Gold-86SE||11-30-2001||04:23 PM||||<BR>Any accident where someone is killed is unfortunate.  But we Fiero guys tend to prize our Fiero for being the safest built cars, just behind the Volvo, from 84 to 88.  And we see something like this and it bothers us more, at least me anyway.<P>Additional news about the driver.<BR>I heard the guy had to be cut from the car, now exactly what that means I don't know, could have been his feet were trapped around the pedals, I am not sure.<P>From what I see in the photo the driver door buckled at the A piller and was pushed down diagonally toward the ground, and the rear of the door was pulled in toward the driver seat.  I might be wrong but that driver seat looks compromised. I wonder if the seat broke loose from the bolts? Another thing, assuming a seat belt was used, I am curious if the seat belt broke?<P>I am just amazed the no one else was hurt at that accident.  From the damage to the Fiero, one would easily think it was really severe to all parties involved.<BR>||||reg||1
