Z||000014||avengador1||11-30-2001||05:08 PM||||I too was seriuosly injured for not wearing my seatbelt back in 1980. It took many years to recover and I still have pain in my ankle. I wasn't even going that fast, maybe about 35 MPH, but when you hit another car head-on and he is doing the same speed you are you get a combined speed effect. In my case 70 MPH. I always wear my seatbelt and don't drive as aggresively as I used to. The injuries I suffered were broken left foot, dislocated right ankle (foot spun 180* around and stuck there),right knee cap split in two(now has a wire holding it together),dislocated left hip(had to wait for two years to find out if I would need a hip replacement or not, luckily I didn't), five broken ribs(from steering wheel), collapsed right lung (got speared by broken ribs), deep cuts to right wrist and hand (went thru dash),nose cut off(only held by the skin on left side of face), fractured skull (sinus damage)my face went thru the windshield, glass in face(still have some pieces I can feel), multiple concussions and internal injuries. It took me almost two years to learn how to walk again and several years of plastic surgery. I still walk with a limp till my ankle muscles warm up. All of this was because I wasn't wearing a belt. If I had been belted my injuries would have been a lot less. My heart goes out to this guy's family and I hope you all out there remember to buckle up. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Mark Matthews||11-30-2001||05:19 PM||||I was in a really bad accident and was 'cut from the car'.  Jaws-of-life saved me.  That and a $7000 helicopter ride to the hospital.  I DID have my seatbelt on, and I do not let anyone ride in my car without their's on as well.  Nor do I ride in a car if I can't where a seatbelt.  Here's link to a picture of the van I was in:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/mark_fglv/Van-Crash.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/mark_fglv/Van-Crash.jpg</A> <P>It's a picture I keep in my wallet, to remind me what can happen...<P>None of the other cars in the picture were involved, that's of it at the tow yard, after I got out of the hospital.  Wasn't my fault either, rear-ended and pushed into on-coming traffic.<P>:edit:  My heart goes out to everyone who knew him.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Mark Matthews (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
